## F4. The spare in handoff's own view
-- no spare:
$ handoff   (the "sessions" part)
  (no such part)
-- a spare that has just been named:
$ handoff   (the "sessions" part)
sessions:
  spare: not listening now (never listened)
-- after quiet_after (2 s here) with no listener:
$ handoff   (the "sessions" part)
sessions:
  spare: not listening now (never listened)
-- while its wait runs:
$ handoff   (the "sessions" part)
  (no such part)
-- a permission prompt in it (Notification hook):
$ handoff   (the "sessions" part)
sessions:
  blocked: the spare's session is at a permission prompt: Claude needs your permission to use Bash, since HH:MM, so it can't cover a stuck seat until you answer it
-- its process ends:
$ handoff   (the "sessions" part)
  (no such part)
-- an Antigravity spare at its cap:
$ handoff   (the "sessions" part)
sessions:
  blocked: the spare can't be woken until you type in its session (Antigravity's 10 wakes used, since HH:MM), so it can't cover a stuck seat
  alerts to the operator (2):
    f4: spare is waiting for your permission: Claude needs your permission to use Bash
    f4: handoff can't wake spare's Antigravity session for new work until you type in it: Antigravity lets hooks continue a turn 10 times in a row.

